 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "And I will yet more nectar deliver,\nTo my own soul and ours.\nIII. The Old Priest's Tale of Redemption\nThere was an old man, that alone\nThe fair Lyre could call to him being,\nIn a richly-moulded chamber,\nWhere the windows showed along\nAn avenue vast with flowers\nAnd lovely gardens profuse;  told\nAll the stories he knew about\nHis life in golden glory before\nThe sudden change from heaven.\nThis same tale is but story,\nBut then it is not untrue story;\nFor, when in springtime ere until\nThree years should come again again,\nThat ageless Spirit arrived\nWith visions and revelations there\nTo all who, like myself, might expect\nThe true fulfilment of mankind,",
